# Cloudflare Workers static-assets redirects.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/
#
# /app/* is the Universal/App Link path space. When the app is installed the OS opens
# the app and the web server is never hit. When it is NOT installed the browser loads
# /app/<route> here, so we serve the single path-aware fallback page for every /app/*
# path with a 200 (proxy/rewrite): the URL stays /app/<route> so the page's script can
# read the route from location.pathname and personalize the message.
#
# The status code 200 = proxy (content served, URL unchanged), NOT a redirect. Splats
# match greedily and are referenced with :splat (unused here; we always serve the one
# page). This rule is scoped to /app/* so the rest of the site (/, /tips/*, /privacy.html,
# /.well-known/*, etc.) is unaffected.
#
# The destination lives at the ROOT (/app-fallback.html), NOT under /app/. If it were under
# /app/ (e.g. /app/index.html), Cloudflare rejects the rule as an infinite loop, because the
# destination itself matches the /app/* source and .html/index stripping would re-trigger it.
# Bare /app (no trailing slash) does not match the /app/* splat, so cover it explicitly.
/app /app-fallback 200
/app/* /app-fallback 200
